{
  "title": { "en": "Inserting" },
  "tray": "machine",
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "Sorting is a program, and a program can be defined by equations. Insertion sort puts the elements one by one into a sorted list."
      }
    }
  ],
  "after": { "en": "Defining a function is writing a program; Simp runs it." },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "sort-ins_1",
      "kind": "define",
      "words": ["everyday", "terms"],
      "step": { "en": "If" },
      "fn": "if",
      "on": 0,
      "rows": [{ "lhs": "if(tt, v, w)", "choices": ["v", "w"] }, { "lhs": "if(ff, v, w)", "choices": ["w", "v"] }],
      "tests": [
        { "term": "if(tt, zero, s(zero))", "value": "zero" },
        { "term": "if(ff, zero, s(zero))", "value": "s(zero)" }
      ],
      "solution": ["v", "w"],
      "naive": ["v", "v"],
      "brief": {
        "en": "Write a right side for every row."
      },
      "hint": [
        { "en": "if c then v else w: v when c is true, w when it is false." }
      ],
      "intro": [
        {
          "t": {
            "en": "A program’s “if” is a function too: one row for each truth value of its condition."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sort-ins_2",
      "kind": "define",
      "words": ["everyday", "terms"],
      "step": { "en": "Inserting" },
      "fn": "ins",
      "on": 1,
      "defs": ["le", "if"],
      "rows": [
        { "lhs": "ins(x, nil)", "choices": ["cons(x, nil)", "nil"] },
        {
          "lhs": "ins(x, cons(y, ys))",
          "choices": [
            "if(le(x, y), cons(x, cons(y, ys)), cons(y, ins(x, ys)))",
            "if(le(x, y), cons(y, ins(x, ys)), cons(x, cons(y, ys)))",
            "cons(x, cons(y, ys))"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "term": "ins(s(zero), cons(zero, cons(s(s(zero)), nil)))",
          "value": "cons(zero, cons(s(zero), cons(s(s(zero)), nil)))"
        },
        { "term": "ins(zero, cons(s(zero), nil))", "value": "cons(zero, cons(s(zero), nil))" },
        { "term": "ins(s(s(zero)), cons(zero, nil))", "value": "cons(zero, cons(s(s(zero)), nil))" }
      ],
      "solution": ["cons(x, nil)", "if(le(x, y), cons(x, cons(y, ys)), cons(y, ins(x, ys)))"],
      "naive": ["cons(x, nil)", "cons(x, cons(y, ys))"],
      "brief": {
        "en": "Write a right side for every row."
      },
      "hint": [{ "en": "Compare x with the first of the list, y." }],
      "intro": [
        {
          "t": {
            "en": "ins puts a number into a sorted list; it takes apart its second argument."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sort-ins_3",
      "kind": "define",
      "words": ["everyday", "terms"],
      "step": { "en": "Sort" },
      "fn": "sort",
      "on": 0,
      "defs": ["le", "if", "ins"],
      "rows": [
        { "lhs": "sort(nil)", "choices": ["nil"] },
        { "lhs": "sort(cons(x, xs))", "choices": ["ins(x, sort(xs))", "cons(x, sort(xs))", "ins(x, xs)"] }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "term": "sort(cons(s(s(zero)), cons(zero, cons(s(zero), nil))))",
          "value": "cons(zero, cons(s(zero), cons(s(s(zero)), nil)))"
        },
        {
          "term": "sort(cons(s(zero), cons(s(zero), cons(zero, nil))))",
          "value": "cons(zero, cons(s(zero), cons(s(zero), nil)))"
        }
      ],
      "solution": ["nil", "ins(x, sort(xs))"],
      "naive": ["nil", "ins(x, xs)"],
      "brief": {
        "en": "Write a right side for every row."
      },
      "hint": [{ "en": "ins wants a sorted list." }]
    },
    {
      "id": "sort-ins_4",
      "kind": "machine",
      "want": "proved",
      "inputs": [{ "name": "in", "label": { "en": "Goal" } }],
      "backtrack": true,
      "words": ["everyday", "terms"],
      "step": { "en": "A few examples" },
      "types": ["list"],
      "defs": ["le", "if", "ins", "sort", "len"],
      "tests": [
        { "goal": "ins(s(zero), cons(zero, cons(s(s(zero)), nil))) = cons(zero, cons(s(zero), cons(s(s(zero)), nil)))" },
        { "goal": "ins(zero, cons(s(zero), nil)) = cons(zero, cons(s(zero), nil))" },
        { "goal": "ins(s(s(zero)), cons(zero, nil)) = cons(zero, cons(s(s(zero)), nil))" }
      ],
      "brief": { "en": "Design a proof assistant that proves every goal." },
      "hint": [{ "en": "The definitions of comparison, if and insert are all needed." }],
      "solution": [
        "c0r0 = math[use=[\"def.0\", \"def.1\", \"def.2\", \"def.3\", \"def.4\", \"def.5\", \"def.6\", \"def.7\", \"def.8\"]]()",
        "c1r0 = refl()",
        "c0 = simp(in, c0r0)",
        "c1 = rule(c0, c1r0)",
        "out <- c1"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
